    "sourceUrl": "https://sansarpetsupply.com/how-to-choose-digestive-friendly-chews-for-your-dog",
    "body": [
      "If your pup is struggling with digestion issues, don’t worry – there are special chews that can help soothe their stomach! In this guide, you’ll learn about the different types of chews available and which ones might be best for your pup’s digestive system.",
      "When shopping for digestion-friendly chews, the most important factor to look for is the ingredients. Chews made with natural and digestible ingredients are ideal for canines who struggle with indigestion. Look for all-natural chews that are made without artificial colors, flavors, or preservatives, as these can cause further upset in your pup’s system. Additionally, avoid products that contain high levels of sugar or salt as these have little nutritional value and can cause digestive upset.",
      "When choosing digestion-friendly treats for your pup, it’s important to look for chews that are free from artificial colors and flavors as these can irritate their stomach. Some treats contain food dyes that can cause allergic reactions or gastrointestinal problems. Avoid any products with FD&C numbers listed on the ingredients label, including red dye #40, blue dye #2, yellow dyes 5 and 6, and green dye #3. Additionally, opt for products without added sugar or salt.",
      "The key to a digestive-friendly chew is picking a non-allergenic source of protein. Foods like beef, chicken, and turkey are common allergens for dogs so instead choose options without these ingredients. Venison, rabbit, yak, duck, bison, and ostrich are all amazing lean sources of protein and your pup will likely love them. Look for chews made from these types of meats or opt for vegetable-based proteins like sweet potatoes.",
      "Chewy treats can be a great addition to your pup’s dental health routine. Not only can they help get rid of plaque but they also give your pooch some mental stimulation by working to completely chew off the treat. Sticks and dental chews are two safe options that can be especially effective when it comes to cleaning teeth since both require more chewing. Additionally, choose chews that don’t break down easily as this allows for more contact between the chew and your pup’s teeth!",
      "While searching for the best type of chew, look for ingredients that can offer your pup health benefits. For example, many dog chews contain natural ingredients like pumpkin, sweet potatoes, and oats that may help soothe your pup’s stomach. Additionally, keep an eye out for omega-3 fatty acids which can help promote healthier skin and a shinier coat! Look for chews that are made with simple, recognizable ingredients, and make sure to check the label in order to pick options that are specifically designed to support your pup’s digestive health."
    ]
